WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.875
Three things follow from that table.

2
00:00:01.875 --> 00:00:06.525
First, nothing in Microsoft Entra
I D speaks Kerberos for a service.

3
00:00:06.525 --> 00:00:11.831
A workload that authenticates with Kerberos
or N T L M to an on-premises resource,

4
00:00:11.831 --> 00:00:17.137
a file share, a SQL Server login mapped
to a Windows account, or a Kerberos-only

5
00:00:17.137 --> 00:00:22.363
application, keeps an Active Directory
identity until that resource changes.

6
00:00:22.363 --> 00:00:27.225
Second, a G M S A is a better
password, not a different protocol.

7
00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:31.755
It's long, random and rotated, but
it still exists, every host allowed

8
00:00:31.755 --> 00:00:36.450
to retrieve it holds it, and it works
only while Active Directory does.

9
00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.457
Third, managed identities
are the end state

10
00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:42.213
only on Azure or on an Arc-enabled server.

11
00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:45.660
So a hybrid workload keeps
its G M S A for Kerberos

12
00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:48.850
and gets a cloud identity
for its cloud calls.

13
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.125
Learn also documents special cases.

14
00:00:51.125 --> 00:00:54.001
Failover clusters don't support G M S As,

15
00:00:54.001 --> 00:00:57.775
though services on the
Cluster service can use one.

16
00:00:57.775 --> 00:01:02.300
In Entra Domain Services, the
K D S root key is pre-created.

17
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:04.718
Cloud Sync's agent runs as a G M S A,

18
00:01:04.718 --> 00:01:09.530
and Connect Sync's account can
be chosen only at installation.
